WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:06.040
Looking back at the weirdest and riskiest
movies of 2019, some were fantastic, and others

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:07.570
just didn't work.

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:11.470
Either way, these films featured plots that
left viewers scratching their heads.

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:14.869
Here are some of the most baffling movies
of 2019.

00:00:14.869 --> 00:00:17.180
Heads up - some light spoilers ahead.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:23.360
Writer-director Ari Aster's Midsommar avoids
many horror tropes to tell its tale of folk

00:00:23.369 --> 00:00:27.990
horror - and Florence Pugh is nothing short
of a powerhouse in the lead role.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:32.150
Midsommar is one of those films where you
can tell things are going to go majorly sideways

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:33.320
from the beginning.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:37.620
Aster loves to leave dangling threads for
his characters - and his audience - to pull

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.480
on, with lots of half-answers sprinkled throughout.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:41.860
"That sounds fun."

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:46.180
Regardless of what your theories about the
movie might be, there are most likely clues

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:50.120
to support them - and plenty of clues that
point in the opposite direction.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:55.460
Velvet Buzzsaw is one of those movies that
makes it tough to truly tell whether what

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:57.140
you're watching is actually any good.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:02.600
It has all the pieces in place, starting with
a solid cast lead by Jake Gyllenhaal and Rene Russo.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:07.880
Dan Gilroy directed it, fresh off the dark
and grossly satisfying Nightcrawler.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:12.979
It centers around artwork coming to life and
murdering critics - and that basically sums

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:13.780
things up.

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:17.620
On the other hand, is anything in Velvet Buzzsaw
really happening?

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:23.060
Or is it all just an extremely meta commentary
on the way we consume and critique art?

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:25.070
What's even going on in this movie?

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:28.560
There are a lot of questions raised and not
a lot of answers given.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:33.140
But if you like watching good actors playing
bizarre characters, Velvet Buzzsaw is for

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:38.600
Very few directors have debuted with their first feature quite like Jordan Peele did

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:40.600
with 2017's Get Out.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:45.680
He had high hopes to live up to with his sophomore
effort, Us, and he delivered another fresh

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.450
thriller with a ton of layers.

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:52.100
"If you wanna get crazy we can get crazy."

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:57.060
It didn't quite strike the same nerve as Get
Out, but it inspired plenty of hot takes on

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:58.140
its release.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:03.500
Everyone in the main cast plays a double role
in the film - their regular selves and their

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:07.540
"Tethered" version, unleashed from the secret
underground society where they've been kept

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:09.230
for who knows how long.

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:14.040
As the film goes on and you learn more about
what the Tethered are, it becomes apparent

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.570
why they're a force to be reckoned with.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:21.810
Lupita Nyong'o steals the show, delivering
an impressive dual performance.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:26.120
Even after you've seen it multiple times,
Us will keep you guessing and have you theorizing

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:27.120
for hours.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:34.640
Robert Eggers followed up his 2015 film The
Witch with 2019's equally perplexing The Lighthouse.

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:40.910
It's shot in black and white and an almost
square aspect ratio - no widescreen here.

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:45.090
It's a two-man show, with Robert Pattinson
and Willem Dafoe playing two men manning a

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:47.820
lighthouse together - and it's completely
bizarre.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:52.410
When you watch The Lighthouse, there are about
50 different ways to interpret it.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:54.740
Maybe everything is literally happening.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:56.370
Maybe only some of it is.

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:58.620
Maybe Pattinson isn't real.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:00.560
Maybe Dafoe isn't!

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:03.930
Unlike The Witch, The Lighthouse never really
gives you any answers.

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:07.620
Still, it's an impressive film that a group
of people could watch at the same time and

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:11.080
all come to wildly different, plausible conclusions.

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:16.550
The Perfection is a body-horror masterpiece
that will have you squirming in your seat.

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:20.400
It's also a film that will keep you guessing
until the very end, even if things do wrap

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.980
up a little more neatly than many of 2019's
weirdest films.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:28.020
The plot centers around two women in a prestigious
music academy.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:33.330
What starts as a simple tale of revenge becomes
more and more insane - it's exploitative and

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:37.390
tough to watch, but it definitely hits the
right buttons for people who are looking for

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:39.160
a bizarre viewing experience.

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:40.840
"Something is wrong.

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:42.840
Something is wrong with me."

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:48.260
Featuring killer performances from both Allison
Williams and Logan Browning, The Perfection

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:51.580
is creepy, weird, and oddly satisfying.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:56.900
One of the best films of 2019 is also one
of its most baffling.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:02.380
Legendary Korean director Bong Joon-Ho's Parasite
is full of twists and turns, and you never

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:04.370
quite know exactly where it's going.

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:09.040
The film starts out as a commentary on wealth
and social class and a story in which one

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:13.450
lower-class family begins to push themselves
into the life and social standing of a much

00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:14.800
wealthier family.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:19.500
About halfway through, however, things take
a dramatic turn and Parasite becomes more

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:24.740
of a horror-thriller as secrets are revealed
and a series of dramatic revelations occur.

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:29.400
Joon-ho employs dark humor so perfectly that
it keeps you off balance.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:34.520
While watching Parasite, you never know if
you should be smiling or just plain horrified.

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:40.400
Not every baffling movie of 2019 was good,
and Serenity never quite gels.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:45.780
That said, it's still worth a watch just for
one particularly memorable and bizarre plot

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:46.560
twist.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:50.140
If you want to see Matthew McConaughey and
Anne Hathaway work their way through some

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:53.640
truly strange material, Serenity is a good
way to do it.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:58.860
After Hathaway's character asks her ex-husband,
played by McConaughey, to murder her current

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:03.370
husband, he wrestles with the idea, and you'll
probably think you know where the plot is

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:04.750
going from there.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:07.030
Fun fact: you don't!

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:11.440
When the twist arrives, odds are pretty good
that you'll find it just doesn't work that well.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:14.000
But man, does it try.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:18.650
Serenity really swings for the fences, and
many of the bizarre plot twists further confuse

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:20.700
things rather than clearing them up.

